WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.893
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:16.163 --> 00:19.416
[theme music playing]

3
00:57.872 --> 00:59.790
Sir, didn't you say you were heading out for a meal?

4
01:00.374 --> 01:01.417
This is important.

5
01:01.917 --> 01:03.252
I need to double-check something.

6
01:04.003 --> 01:06.171
-Huh? -You're the one who started it, though.

7
01:06.255 --> 01:08.841
["Drawn" by THAMA playing]

8
01:29.945 --> 01:30.821
-[music stops] -[Jae-hee gasps]

9
01:31.697 --> 01:34.116
You crazy… You want me to smack you right now?

10
01:34.199 --> 01:35.492
Go right ahead,

11
01:36.410 --> 01:38.203
though I'm pretty sure you don't have the balls.

12
01:38.287 --> 01:39.747
-[tense, whimsical music playing] -Uh…

13
01:39.830 --> 01:41.248
And if you recall,

14
01:41.624 --> 01:45.002
a certain someone got drunk the other day and kissed me against my will.

15
01:45.085 --> 01:47.671
-That was just-- -[Yi-jun] Ever since then,

16
01:47.755 --> 01:49.548
I've been feeling unusually flustered.

17
01:49.632 --> 01:50.883
Anxious.

18
01:53.344 --> 01:54.803
I thought this over,

19
01:55.596 --> 01:56.847
and I've made a decision.

20
01:57.598 --> 01:58.891
[deep exhale]

21
01:59.183 --> 02:01.060
[tense, whimsical music continues]

22
02:03.729 --> 02:05.481
All these weeks we've spent together,

23
02:07.274 --> 02:08.275
it was a waste of time.

24
02:08.359 --> 02:09.944
I'm disappointed in you.

25
02:10.027 --> 02:10.986
[music fades]

26
02:18.953 --> 02:21.830
Uh, how… how could he believe that?

27
02:24.083 --> 02:25.376
Is he out of his mind?

28
02:27.920 --> 02:28.754
[sighs]

29
02:28.837 --> 02:31.715
[Jae-hee's dad] There are times in life when our feelings for someone

30
02:31.799 --> 02:35.386
charge headfirst into us like a raging bull.

31
02:35.469 --> 02:40.224
When people who are new to dating start to see signs of love in the air,

32
02:40.307 --> 02:41.809
they reject those feelings.

33
02:41.892 --> 02:44.186
Why? Their survival instinct.

34
02:44.269 --> 02:45.104
PROFESSOR ROMANCE MYEONGHO-DONG HEARTTHROB'S LOVE TALK

35
02:45.187 --> 02:48.023
Yeah. They think, "What if I lose?" Huh?

36
02:48.107 --> 02:51.485
They think it's too risky, and they could get screwed.

37
02:51.902 --> 02:53.821
And that's when they figure it out.

38
02:54.613 --> 02:57.241
They start noticing a lot of their personal flaws.

39
02:57.324 --> 03:00.411
They start acknowledging their contradictions,

40
03:00.494 --> 03:02.788
inconsistencies between words and actions.

41
03:02.871 --> 03:04.873
Hey, why did he follow me here anyway?

42
03:05.624 --> 03:08.627
[gasps] Uh, shouldn't you be heading home?

43
03:09.044 --> 03:10.295
Since I'm so generous,

44
03:10.379 --> 03:12.631
I'll give you a chance to atone for what you did.

45
03:12.715 --> 03:14.800
-[gasps softly] -Buy me dinner.

46
03:14.883 --> 03:16.176
[Jae-hee] Why should I buy you dinner?

47
03:16.802 --> 03:18.220
I saved you from falling face first,

48
03:18.303 --> 03:21.223
only for you to hit the back of my knee, pin me down on the ground,

49
03:21.306 --> 03:23.017
and on top of everything,

50
03:23.100 --> 03:25.352
you dared to put your lips against my lips.

51
03:25.436 --> 03:26.478
I know.

52
03:26.562 --> 03:29.773
Listen, that was a mistake. You do realize that.

53
03:29.857 --> 03:31.817
And that's why you'll get a chance to apologize.

54
03:32.526 --> 03:33.819
Fine. I'll get you dinner tomorrow.

55
03:33.902 --> 03:36.238
-No, today. I'm hungry now. -[gasps]

56
03:37.573 --> 03:39.241
-[sighs] -[whimsical music playing]

57
03:39.324 --> 03:41.326
Who was that guy earlier?

58
03:41.410 --> 03:42.661
Was he a friend?

59
03:42.745 --> 03:44.121
Careful who you associate with.

60
03:44.204 --> 03:47.207
I only say this because you're like a little brother who needs protecting.

61
03:47.291 --> 03:49.668
Actually, you should bring him over.

62
03:49.752 --> 03:52.004
-I wanna meet him. I-- -Let's go eat now.

63
03:52.963 --> 03:54.965
I wanna buy you dinner, sir. Yep.

64
03:56.675 --> 03:58.886
EPISODE 6

65
03:58.969 --> 04:00.429
[toy laser swords whooshing]

66
04:06.602 --> 04:08.520
[slurping]

67
04:08.604 --> 04:10.439
[munching]

68
04:11.648 --> 04:12.733
Why aren't you eating?

69
04:13.650 --> 04:14.568
Is something wrong?

70
04:14.651 --> 04:17.321
Given the quality, why not just go to a convenience store?

71
04:18.572 --> 04:20.657
That was an option I did consider.

72
04:20.741 --> 04:22.743
I just thought you wanted to lie low.

73
04:27.081 --> 04:28.999
What kind of cuisine do you like, sir?

74
04:29.083 --> 04:30.876
I'd like you to be less interested.

75
04:30.959 --> 04:32.503
-[banging on window] -[thug 1] Hey, hey!

76
04:32.586 --> 04:34.630
-I'm talking to you, asshole. -[tense, whimsical music playing]

77
04:34.713 --> 04:37.800
But I will say, what I don't like is this kind of junk food,

78
04:37.883 --> 04:39.676
oozing a lot of toxic oil and fat.

79
04:39.760 --> 04:42.179
Uh, sir, what's your 100-meter dash record?

80
04:42.262 --> 04:43.555
I'm not gonna answer that question.

81
04:43.639 --> 04:46.350
-I'm not in the mood for a run. -That's too bad.

82
04:46.433 --> 04:48.393
-Guess I'll do it on my own. -What?

83
04:48.477 --> 04:50.062
-[banging on window] -[jaunty, syncopated piano music playing]

84
04:50.145 --> 04:52.314
He's in there! Hey, buddy, got something to say?

85
04:52.397 --> 04:53.357
Hey, wanna die?

86
04:53.440 --> 04:54.775
-[grunts] -Whoa! Sir!

87
04:54.858 --> 04:57.653
[groans]

88
04:59.947 --> 05:01.406
[music fades]

89
05:02.324 --> 05:03.534
I think they want you dead.

90
05:04.118 --> 05:05.077
Is this something you're aware of?

91
05:05.160 --> 05:06.245
It isn't, no.

92
05:06.328 --> 05:08.914
Listen, go out to the intersection and get a cab.

93
05:08.997 --> 05:10.499
They'll have the premium ones.

94
05:10.582 --> 05:13.335
Don't come out for five… no, ten minutes.

95
05:13.418 --> 05:14.545
-Special Forces. -[thug 1] Where did he go?

96
05:14.628 --> 05:16.338
-Where's that punk? -[thug 2] Hey, where is he?

97
05:16.421 --> 05:18.048
-[thug 3] That way. -Where the hell did he go?

98
05:18.132 --> 05:19.716
Man, sneaky little prick.

99
05:19.800 --> 05:21.009
[thug 3] Sir, he's over there.

100
05:21.093 --> 05:22.928
-[thug 1] Hurry up, guys. Right there. -Ugh, what the heck did he…

101
05:23.011 --> 05:25.013
[upbeat tense music playing]

102
05:25.097 --> 05:25.931
[thug 1] Right out there!

103
05:27.558 --> 05:29.893
-[thug 3] You're a dead man. -[thug 1] Over here. This way, guys.

104
05:29.977 --> 05:30.853
[thug exclaims]

105
05:30.936 --> 05:32.020
[music fades]

106
05:34.398 --> 05:35.691
[indistinct chatter]

107
05:37.818 --> 05:39.653
[sucks teeth]

108
05:40.320 --> 05:43.073
Well, just so you know, I had a full course meal planned and everything.

109
05:43.157 --> 05:46.618
Bone-in haejangguk, fried rice, some toppings.

110
05:47.411 --> 05:48.745
That's full course, right?

111
05:48.829 --> 05:50.455
[chuckles] So does that mean you're…

112
05:50.956 --> 05:53.041
willing to forgive my sins after all?

113
05:53.125 --> 05:55.669
A meal is a meal. A sin is a sin.

114
05:55.752 --> 05:58.714
So I'll buy you some food, then you'll put me on trial.

115
05:58.797 --> 06:02.426
Is this like when cops buy you gukbap right before your interrogation?

116
06:02.509 --> 06:05.345
If you wanna confess before we eat, you have the floor.

117
06:05.429 --> 06:06.680
Ugh. [sighs]

118
06:07.639 --> 06:09.183
God. [inhales deeply]

119
06:09.266 --> 06:12.269
I could make the excuse "My phone had just broken."

120
06:13.937 --> 06:17.357
But I happen to be a lawyer, so I know how perjury works.

121
06:17.441 --> 06:21.028
Given the situation I was in, I couldn't answer, so I hung up.

122
06:21.111 --> 06:23.739
There are many situations where one can't take calls.

123
06:23.822 --> 06:24.907
What was yours, I wonder?

124
06:24.990 --> 06:26.366
Uh, you know.

125
06:26.450 --> 06:27.868
-[chuckles] -[bottle cap opens]

126
06:27.951 --> 06:29.870
Yeah, so in my particular case,

127
06:29.953 --> 06:31.705
I just happened to be meeting up with someone.

128
06:33.123 --> 06:34.458
[beer fizzing]

129
06:34.541 --> 06:35.751
Yoon Na-jung, I imagine.

130
06:36.668 --> 06:39.463
[intriguing, tense music playing]

131
06:41.882 --> 06:44.343
Secretarial chat is powerful, you know.

132
06:45.719 --> 06:46.678
Fine.

133
06:46.762 --> 06:48.305
[inhales deeply]

134
06:48.388 --> 06:49.848
I'll be honest with you.

135
06:50.933 --> 06:52.851
I'll tell you why she and I were meeting,

136
06:52.935 --> 06:54.394
but before I do,

137
06:54.478 --> 06:57.356
I'd like it if you could tell me something.

138
07:04.321 --> 07:05.948
Concerning Han Eun-young's desk,

139
07:07.950 --> 07:09.117
why'd you replace it?

140
07:09.660 --> 07:12.996
[intriguing, tense music swells]

141
07:13.080 --> 07:14.748
-[upbeat music playing] -[thug 1] There he is!

142
07:14.831 --> 07:17.668
Follow him! Run him down! Hurry, faster!

143
07:17.751 --> 07:20.337
Whoa! [panting]

144
07:20.420 --> 07:21.838
-[thug 1] He's going that way. -[thug 4] Come on, over here.

145
07:21.922 --> 07:23.715
[thug 2] Hey, got it.

146
07:23.799 --> 07:25.425
[Jae-hee panting]

147
07:25.509 --> 07:27.094
[thug 5] Over there! He's going that way!

148
07:28.095 --> 07:30.430
Down the alleyway, come on! Hurry!

149
07:30.514 --> 07:31.765
Don't let him get away!

150
07:31.848 --> 07:33.558
-[music stops] -[man on TV] Why're you like this?

151
07:33.642 --> 07:34.768
-I said I'm sorry! -[woman on TV] Whatever!

152
07:34.851 --> 07:35.852
-Get out! I said leave! -[man on TV] Fine, I'll go!

153
07:35.936 --> 07:37.688
[owner] My goodness, this show is so frustrating.

154
07:37.771 --> 07:38.897
You know what I mean?

155
07:39.690 --> 07:42.276
This idiot knows nothing about women.

156
07:42.359 --> 07:44.444
-He's an absolute airhead. -[man on TV] Okay, I'm going!

157
07:44.528 --> 07:46.488
That's right! I want you out!

158
07:47.114 --> 07:49.032
I think this guy should go if she wants him gone.

159
07:49.116 --> 07:50.284
He's embarrassing himself.

160
07:50.367 --> 07:51.785
What does she want, for him to refuse?

161
07:52.828 --> 07:54.830
[whimsical music playing]

162
07:57.833 --> 07:59.209
[mouths words]

163
08:01.253 --> 08:03.297
-[light, comedic music playing] -Does she really come here alone?

164
08:03.380 --> 08:04.965
I'm the first guy she brought, right?

165
08:05.048 --> 08:07.259
[owner] If you wanna make it work with that cutie,

166
08:07.342 --> 08:10.178
there, look, you should start studying that.

167
08:10.262 --> 08:12.139
She's always watching this, she's hooked.

168
08:12.222 --> 08:15.142
[scoffs] Really? Come on.

169
08:15.225 --> 08:17.311
Yeah. [chuckles]

170
08:17.394 --> 08:20.188
Wow, you really don't know a thing about that girl.

171
08:21.023 --> 08:23.650
Put those potatoes back and the cabbage.

172
08:23.734 --> 08:26.194
Ah, okay. I can only have the meat, or--

173
08:26.278 --> 08:28.155
-Beer as well. -Why?

174
08:28.238 --> 08:30.240
-Soju. -Huh?

175
08:30.324 --> 08:32.951
[owner] Put it away before she's back from the bathroom.

176
08:33.035 --> 08:35.037
[light, comedic music continues]

177
08:38.165 --> 08:39.166
[music ends]

178
08:41.668 --> 08:42.836
[refrigerator door slides open]

179
08:43.462 --> 08:46.256
I heard you're into K-dramas and hate vegetables.

180
08:47.549 --> 08:49.718
I don't get it. How does the restaurant owner know you

181
08:49.801 --> 08:51.386
better than I do? That kinda hurts.

182
08:51.470 --> 08:54.306
Wow, you really have a lot of questions.

183
08:54.389 --> 08:57.059
'Cause you never wanna give me real answers.

184
08:59.394 --> 09:00.937
Why don't you change that?

185
09:01.563 --> 09:04.775
Han Eun-young's desk, what happened there?

186
09:05.609 --> 09:09.988
Why don't you tell me why you're so interested in that desk?

187
09:10.072 --> 09:10.947
What's going on there?

188
09:11.031 --> 09:12.699
[tense music playing]

189
09:12.783 --> 09:13.992
Yeah, but I asked you first.

190
09:14.076 --> 09:17.287
You know the saying that wells are dug by whoever's thirsty?

191
09:18.747 --> 09:20.207
Whoever's more curious…

192
09:21.333 --> 09:22.584
will find out first.

193
09:23.585 --> 09:27.631
[panting]

194
09:27.714 --> 09:29.091
-[Jae-hee] Whoa. -[thugs shouting indistinctly]

195
09:29.174 --> 09:30.592
-[Jae-hee] No, wait! -We got you, buddy.

196
09:30.675 --> 09:32.052
-[panting] -[thug 3] That's right, it's over.

197
09:32.135 --> 09:33.470
Hey, there. I've missed you.

198
09:33.553 --> 09:34.638
Oh, did you really?

199
09:34.721 --> 09:36.264
Come on, get over here.

200
09:36.348 --> 09:38.892
-[thug 3] You're fucking dead. -[thug 4] Come on. You heard me.

201
09:38.975 --> 09:39.893
[thug 1] Move it, bro.

202
09:39.976 --> 09:43.730
Don't do it, don't do it, don't do it! Don't do it! Don't do it! Don't do it!

203
09:43.814 --> 09:44.981
[Jae-hee] I'm sorry, Captain.

204
09:45.065 --> 09:46.608
[thugs] Whoa, whoa, whoa!

205
09:46.691 --> 09:48.735
-It's been a minute, huh? -Whoa, whoa!

206
09:48.819 --> 09:50.445
Nice try. I came prepared.

207
09:50.529 --> 09:51.780
Ah, cute.

208
09:51.863 --> 09:53.698
[exclaims]

209
09:53.782 --> 09:55.075
It's not working.

210
09:55.784 --> 09:56.910
[thug 2] Oh, there's no water. [chuckles]

211
09:56.993 --> 09:58.328
-Jeez. -[thug 2] What now?

212
09:58.412 --> 10:00.163
Hey, guys, get your weapons ready.

213
10:00.247 --> 10:01.957
-[thugs] Yes, sir! -That's messed up. How many are there?

214
10:02.040 --> 10:03.875
One, two, three, four, five, six…

215
10:03.959 --> 10:05.627
[Yi-jun] Everybody freeze!

216
10:08.422 --> 10:10.382
[tense music playing]

217
10:16.721 --> 10:18.932
Oh, God. Stop it, sir!

218
10:20.183 --> 10:22.185
[dramatic tense music playing]

219
10:23.395 --> 10:26.398
[toy laser sword humming]

220
10:28.775 --> 10:30.652
Don't, sir. Not now.

221
10:34.364 --> 10:35.490
Wow.

222
10:37.742 --> 10:39.619
[toy laser sword hums]

223
10:42.164 --> 10:43.540
[thugs] Whoa!

224
10:44.249 --> 10:45.208
This guy's gonna get it.

225
10:45.292 --> 10:47.127
What the heck? You didn't take a taxi?

226
10:47.210 --> 10:48.462
You're gonna get hurt.

227
10:48.545 --> 10:51.089
Go over there, sit down, and pretend you're invisible, okay?

228
10:51.173 --> 10:52.841
[thug 4] Hey, pretty boy.

229
10:53.884 --> 10:55.385
-[toy laser sword hums] -[thug sighs]

230
10:55.469 --> 10:56.803
Careful with that toy there.

231
10:56.887 --> 10:58.180
-Looks dangerous. -[thugs laughing]

232
10:59.181 --> 11:00.265
Watch it.

233
11:00.348 --> 11:02.601
-[solemn, heroic music playing] -[grunts in pain]

234
11:02.684 --> 11:04.519
-[screaming in pain] -What is that thing? What are you doing?

235
11:04.603 --> 11:05.604
-What? -Don't get near it!

236
11:05.687 --> 11:06.855
Stay away!

237
11:06.938 --> 11:09.107
What was that? Where'd you learn that?

238
11:09.191 --> 11:10.734
-Damn. -[indistinct thug chatter]

239
11:10.817 --> 11:13.069
When you compliment someone, it sounds like an insult.

240
11:13.153 --> 11:15.530
That's 'cause that was an insult.

241
11:15.614 --> 11:17.699
-Hey, let's mess them up! -[thug 6] Come on, boss.

242
11:17.782 --> 11:20.035
-[solemn, heroic music continues] -[toy laser sword whooshes]

243
11:20.118 --> 11:23.997
[thugs groaning in pain]

244
11:29.044 --> 11:31.922
[grunting]

245
11:35.217 --> 11:37.469
-[grunting] -[Jae-hee gasps]

246
11:39.095 --> 11:40.430
[panting]

247
11:40.514 --> 11:41.765
[gasps]

248
11:41.848 --> 11:43.975
[grunts, screams in pain]

249
11:44.059 --> 11:46.895
[thug 5 screams] My hand! Damn, that hurts!

250
11:46.978 --> 11:49.814
[upbeat music playing]

251
11:54.236 --> 11:55.529
I don't get it.

252
11:55.612 --> 11:57.113
I've never seen you lift a finger.

253
11:57.197 --> 11:58.782
I told you this.

254
11:58.865 --> 12:00.825
It's not that I can't, I just don't want to.

255
12:01.826 --> 12:05.205
-[upbeat music continues] -[thugs grunting in pain]

256
12:12.629 --> 12:14.047
-You bastard! -[muttering]

257
12:14.839 --> 12:16.258
[screams in pain]

258
12:16.591 --> 12:17.467
Oh, my gosh.

259
12:17.551 --> 12:19.386
-Are you okay, sir? Huh? -I'm fine.

260
12:19.469 --> 12:20.387
Let me look.

261
12:20.470 --> 12:22.973
[gasps] Oh, blood. Geez.

262
12:23.056 --> 12:24.140
Did you hit a civilian?

263
12:24.224 --> 12:25.392
-Here. -Stop. I'm fine.

264
12:25.475 --> 12:26.476
Over here.

265
12:26.893 --> 12:29.771
Now, you be a good boy and stay put for a little bit.

266
12:29.854 --> 12:31.481
Just sit back and enjoy the show.

267
12:31.565 --> 12:33.567
-I said I'm fine. -Mm-mm.

268
12:35.151 --> 12:36.653
As for these guys,

269
12:36.736 --> 12:40.448
-[chuckles] I'll wrap this up in a few. -I'm not even that hurt!

270
12:41.241 --> 12:42.450
Special Forces!

271
12:42.534 --> 12:45.620
You're gonna get it, you sleazy motherforkers.

272
12:45.704 --> 12:47.080
You ready? You ready?

273
12:47.664 --> 12:48.665
[thugs and Jae-hee scream]

274
12:49.249 --> 12:50.083
Motherforkers?

275
12:50.166 --> 12:51.585
[thuds]

276
12:51.668 --> 12:53.628
-[grunts] -[thudding]

277
12:53.712 --> 12:54.754
[groans]

278
12:55.255 --> 12:56.631
-Stop it! -[Jae-hee screams]

279
12:57.257 --> 12:59.467
[upbeat music continues]

280
12:59.551 --> 13:02.012
Bring it! [grunts]

281
13:02.095 --> 13:04.431
-[thug screaming in pain] -Guess he's been holding back on me.

282
13:06.224 --> 13:07.517
[grunting]

283
13:07.601 --> 13:11.271
Your friend, what a cool dude.

284
13:11.354 --> 13:13.356
[Jae-hee] That's right, you bi-yatch.

285
13:13.440 --> 13:15.734
He's so cool, it's scary! [chuckles]

286
13:15.817 --> 13:17.861
-He's my secretary. -[Jae-hee] Hey, you! Get back here!

287
13:17.944 --> 13:18.903
[thug 2] No way.

288
13:18.987 --> 13:20.322
Whoa, whoa, get back, don't!

289
13:20.405 --> 13:21.531
-No! No! -[screams]

290
13:21.615 --> 13:23.199
[music fades]

291
13:23.700 --> 13:25.702
That's the last number Eun-young called.

292
13:26.411 --> 13:28.872
[Captain Park] Good. Let's move on to her text messages now.

293
13:28.955 --> 13:29.914
Right.

294
13:31.124 --> 13:33.251
Come on, what are we, secret agents?

295
13:33.668 --> 13:36.254
So we're investigating, but can't talk about it at all.

296
13:36.338 --> 13:37.339
We found the phone,

297
13:37.422 --> 13:38.673
-but we're not allowed to tell anyone. -[system voice] The number you have dialed

298
13:38.757 --> 13:39.924
is unavailable.

299
13:40.091 --> 13:41.885
Secret agents get fame and glory at least.

300
13:41.968 --> 13:45.305
Yeah, exactly. They go down as heroes in the end.

301
13:45.764 --> 13:49.643
You, Bong-yi, on the other hand, you're just gonna get yelled at.

302
13:49.726 --> 13:51.061
Shut it.

303
13:51.144 --> 13:52.771
[Wan-gu] My grandma had this theory,

304
13:52.854 --> 13:55.732
the name you're given is what dictates your path in life.

305
13:55.815 --> 13:56.816
Drop it.

306
13:56.900 --> 13:59.486
But Bong-yi sounds like bakbong, meaning no money.

307
13:59.569 --> 14:01.279
[quirky music playing]

308
14:01.363 --> 14:03.323
You caught that?

309
14:03.406 --> 14:04.324
How the heck did you do that?

310
14:04.407 --> 14:06.117
-All right, someone's about to get it. -[grunting]

311
14:06.201 --> 14:08.662
-This is long overdue. -[grunts] That feels great. Seriously.

312
14:08.745 --> 14:10.955
-Oh, yeah? How about this? -He's really getting in there good.

313
14:11.039 --> 14:11.873
-[Wan-gu] A little to the left. -Hold on.

314
14:11.956 --> 14:13.041
-Huh? -Hm?

315
14:16.461 --> 14:18.171
-Code One. -Huh?

316
14:18.296 --> 14:19.589
-[sirens wailing] -[Wan-gu] Code One?

317
14:19.673 --> 14:20.715
[gasps]

318
14:20.799 --> 14:21.966
[Captain Park groans]

319
14:22.050 --> 14:25.053
How does a detective get hauled off to the police station?

320
14:25.136 --> 14:27.013
Whatever, put her behind bars.

321
14:27.097 --> 14:30.016
[Wan-gu] Come on, we can't do that. We gotta get her out of there.

322
14:30.100 --> 14:32.435
If her cover's blown, we're screwed.

323
14:33.228 --> 14:34.104
Which station is it?

324
14:35.647 --> 14:37.857
From what I can tell, it's in our neighborhood.

325
14:37.941 --> 14:39.442
Yoon Yi-jun knows your face, Bong-yi.

326
14:40.235 --> 14:41.361
I should go.

327
14:43.488 --> 14:44.948
[gasps] Hang on.

328
14:45.031 --> 14:46.825
What if I'm cleaning the bathroom and he comes in?

329
14:46.908 --> 14:48.076
[Captain Park] God!

330
14:49.202 --> 14:51.538
Ugh, you guys, seriously, I… I can't deal with this.

331
14:51.621 --> 14:53.373
[thug] Why? I didn't do anything.

332
14:53.456 --> 14:54.916
-He threw it. -[overlapping chatter]

333
14:54.999 --> 14:57.711
I'm telling you, those guys did that.

334
14:57.794 --> 15:00.547
-They hit us. They broke a lot of stuff. -[slams table]

335
15:00.630 --> 15:02.590
Can all of you shut up for one second?

336
15:02.924 --> 15:04.718
[thug 3] Those guys better not get away with this.

337
15:04.801 --> 15:06.928
They sweet-talked their way out of that.

338
15:07.011 --> 15:10.390
Oh, okay, so, let me see if I got this right.

339
15:10.473 --> 15:13.059
The members of a fishing gang, whose middleman

340
15:13.143 --> 15:15.770
you got arrested, tracked you down to get revenge.

341
15:15.854 --> 15:19.023
There was a fight, and that's how he ended up looking like this.

342
15:19.107 --> 15:20.400
That was a perfect summary.

343
15:21.484 --> 15:24.070
-So if you don't mind, we'll be going. -[officer] Hang on, sir.

344
15:24.154 --> 15:27.657
I think you severely underestimate the intricacies of police bureaucracy.

345
15:28.283 --> 15:29.284
[Jae-hee] No, I do not.

346
15:29.367 --> 15:31.244
That's why I'm crawling out of my skin right now.

347
15:33.204 --> 15:34.414
[chuckles]

348
15:34.831 --> 15:36.958
[spacey, quirky music playing]

349
15:37.584 --> 15:38.543
Sir, hello?

350
15:38.626 --> 15:41.129
I'd rather you not be spacing out during questioning.

351
15:44.132 --> 15:45.175
[Jae-hee] Are you okay, sir?

352
15:46.050 --> 15:49.554
[gasps] Oh, blood. They hit you there? Geez.

353
15:49.637 --> 15:52.015
Now you be a good boy and take a seat here.

354
15:52.098 --> 15:53.183
Stay put.

355
15:53.683 --> 15:56.019
Kick back and enjoy the show, huh?

356
15:56.102 --> 15:57.437
Bring it on. Bring it!

357
15:58.938 --> 16:00.940
[spacey, quirky music continues]

358
16:01.024 --> 16:02.484
Oh!

359
16:02.567 --> 16:05.069
I guess whatever you're thinking about is making you blush.

360
16:06.279 --> 16:07.447
That's so cute. [chuckles]

361
16:08.698 --> 16:10.074
[clears throat]

362
16:10.408 --> 16:11.951
You been drinking or something?

363
16:12.035 --> 16:12.994
Uh, not at all.

364
16:13.077 --> 16:15.622
As you can see, he's in a weird place right now.

365
16:15.705 --> 16:16.873
We should get him to the ER.

366
16:16.956 --> 16:19.334
We're not going anywhere. I demand justice.

367
16:19.417 --> 16:21.085
[Yi-jun] Round up my legal team.

368
16:21.711 --> 16:24.506
If we do that, the press will show up and this'll be all over the internet.

369
16:24.589 --> 16:26.090
-Please stop it. -That's enough.

370
16:26.424 --> 16:27.592
I'll handle this.

371
16:28.551 --> 16:30.804
Oh, what are you doing?

372
16:30.887 --> 16:32.096
I said enough.

373
16:32.639 --> 16:33.723
Why are you interfering?

374
16:33.807 --> 16:35.475
I'm just worried for you.

375
16:36.059 --> 16:37.560
[Jae-hee] I'm just worried for you.

376
16:38.561 --> 16:39.604
Worried?

377
16:39.687 --> 16:42.232
[Jae-hee] Well, worried for me.

378
16:42.315 --> 16:44.025
So, please, just cooperate. Come on.

379
16:44.526 --> 16:45.693
[officer] Sir, listen.

380
16:45.777 --> 16:47.904
I'd be a little more worried if I were you,

381
16:47.987 --> 16:50.532
because actually even self-defensive action

382
16:50.615 --> 16:52.116
can be classified as an assault.

383
16:52.200 --> 16:54.327
So to follow procedure, here's what I need from you,

384
16:54.828 --> 16:56.746
ID number and your name.

385
16:59.541 --> 17:00.875
[sighs]

386
17:02.710 --> 17:04.546
Oh, excuse me, sir.

387
17:04.629 --> 17:06.381
Can I have a second with you?

388
17:06.464 --> 17:08.049
Just a second.

389
17:08.132 --> 17:10.552
[officer] Oh, yeah, sure. Go on then.

390
17:11.052 --> 17:12.679
I need to talk to the chief of police.

391
17:12.762 --> 17:14.222
-[officer] Ah. -There's something I need.

392
17:14.305 --> 17:15.849
Oh, you want to talk to the chief of police?

393
17:15.932 --> 17:17.183
Yes, the chief.

394
17:17.267 --> 17:19.143
[laughs]

395
17:19.227 --> 17:21.896
You want to speak to the manager? Huh?

396
17:21.980 --> 17:23.398
That crap doesn't work on me.

397
17:23.481 --> 17:26.150
Our chief doesn't live anywhere around here.

398
17:26.234 --> 17:27.277
Want me to call my lawyer?

399
17:27.360 --> 17:29.529
[hesitates]

400
17:29.612 --> 17:32.323
Even if you do, we still need to know who you two are.

401
17:32.407 --> 17:34.158
So why don't you just show me your ID?

402
17:34.242 --> 17:36.703
-It'll only take a second. -[playful, tense music playing]

403
17:36.786 --> 17:39.080
Name and resident number.

404
17:39.163 --> 17:40.540
Let's get this over with.

405
17:43.835 --> 17:45.503
-[Captain Park growls] -[tense music playing]

406
17:45.587 --> 17:48.131
I told you not to run off like that!

407
17:48.214 --> 17:49.924
[sighs]

408
17:53.011 --> 17:56.556
-Kang Jae-hee. -[officer] Jae…

409
17:56.639 --> 17:58.141
-[Jae-hee] Hee. -[officer] Hee.

410
17:59.976 --> 18:01.144
[Jae-hee] Yes.

411
18:01.936 --> 18:03.229
Nine, seven, zero…

412
18:04.522 --> 18:07.025
-eight, one, two. -What was that?

413
18:07.108 --> 18:09.611
[suspenseful music playing]

414
18:09.694 --> 18:12.488
Nine, seven, zero…

415
18:12.572 --> 18:14.032
-eight, one… -[door opens]

416
18:18.119 --> 18:19.287
Hi. Can I help you, sir?

417
18:20.413 --> 18:22.415
[suspenseful music continues]

418
18:28.379 --> 18:29.380
[music ends]

419
18:32.258 --> 18:33.426
I'm sorry, Seok-jin.

420
18:33.509 --> 18:35.219
My father's Chief Cho's boss.

421
18:36.220 --> 18:37.555
Why'd you bring Yi-jun back here?

422
18:37.639 --> 18:38.848
Oh, well,

423
18:39.223 --> 18:42.727
I was just trying to stop him from asking too many questions about you, and then…

424
18:44.437 --> 18:45.855
I should've thought this over. [sighs]

425
18:49.192 --> 18:50.401
[Seok-jin sighs]

426
18:51.152 --> 18:52.195
Get this looked at.

427
18:53.279 --> 18:54.238
Send him home and come back.

428
18:54.322 --> 18:55.323
Yep.

429
19:03.623 --> 19:06.209
ARMY GO JAE-DEOK ARMY KANG JAE-HEE

430
19:06.292 --> 19:08.252
[indistinct chatter]

431
19:11.130 --> 19:14.133
[somber piano music playing]

432
19:35.780 --> 19:38.533
What do you think? Should I call up Mr. Jung right now, sir?

433
19:39.575 --> 19:40.576
Where do you live?

434
19:41.285 --> 19:44.163
Uh, well, I, uh, do live near here.

435
19:45.081 --> 19:47.375
Okay. Then let's take a walk.

436
19:48.584 --> 19:51.087
[somber piano music swells]

437
19:54.716 --> 19:56.592
[music fades]

438
19:58.052 --> 19:59.345
You dropped this earlier.

439
19:59.929 --> 20:01.222
ARMY GO JAE-DEOK ARMY KANG JAE-HEE

440
20:06.769 --> 20:09.355
What's with that other name? Who's that?

441
20:11.649 --> 20:12.817
Can I not answer that?

442
20:13.317 --> 20:14.777
Can I ask something else?

443
20:16.487 --> 20:17.488
Who is that guy?

444
20:18.281 --> 20:20.199
I saw you two together outside of the office.

445
20:20.283 --> 20:23.453
[gentle, tense music playing]

446
20:28.750 --> 20:29.876
He's just an old friend.

447
20:29.959 --> 20:31.502
An old friend?

448
20:32.795 --> 20:35.882
Hey, your fencing looked great earlier. Where'd you learn that?

449
20:37.175 --> 20:38.217
You're doing what you do.

450
20:38.301 --> 20:40.303
I know you're trying to change the subject.

451
20:41.929 --> 20:45.224
You don't wanna answer, so you're trying to distract me with more questions.

452
20:47.810 --> 20:50.146
Well, anyway, this is me.

453
21:00.239 --> 21:01.449
[Si-hyun sighs]

454
21:05.995 --> 21:07.789
Hey, there you go.

455
21:08.956 --> 21:10.625
You're right. I'm thirstier.

456
21:12.085 --> 21:14.504
The reason I've been so interested in who replaced the desk--

457
21:14.587 --> 21:16.214
I have to admit something.

458
21:16.798 --> 21:18.424
There's a reason I approached you.

459
21:20.093 --> 21:22.637
Ever since you told Mr. Kang I was boring,

460
21:23.346 --> 21:26.099
and at the nightclub, I was pursuing you.

461
21:27.725 --> 21:28.684
What's the reason?

462
21:29.185 --> 21:32.605
The fact that you're asking that tells me everything I need.

463
21:34.273 --> 21:36.400
I didn't fake everything, though.

464
21:37.110 --> 21:40.738
Whenever you were nice to me, it made me reconsider.

465
21:42.156 --> 21:44.408
Anyway, we should stop this.

466
21:45.284 --> 21:47.286
[melancholic piano music playing]

467
21:47.620 --> 21:48.579
You wanna stop it?

468
21:54.085 --> 21:56.671
Yes. This is where it ends.

469
22:00.591 --> 22:03.052
[melancholic piano music continues]

470
22:17.483 --> 22:18.484
[music ends]

471
22:24.240 --> 22:26.117
[unsettling music playing]

472
22:34.917 --> 22:39.505
[phone buzzes]

473
22:41.883 --> 22:43.301
This is Lee Hye-jung.

474
22:43.384 --> 22:45.136
[Captain Park] This is the Seoul Metropolitan Police.

475
22:45.219 --> 22:46.554
You had a call with Han Eun-young,

476
22:46.637 --> 22:48.389
the victim in the Taekang Group murder case,

477
22:48.472 --> 22:50.099
around February 5th, correct?

478
22:51.100 --> 22:53.102
[suspenseful music playing]

479
22:58.065 --> 22:59.692
Aside from me, who else knows

480
23:00.526 --> 23:03.779
that Mr. Yoon's been digging into the slush fund?

481
23:07.575 --> 23:11.120
Han Eun-young, I'm asking if you told anyone else,

482
23:11.204 --> 23:12.997
and if so, I need to know who.

483
23:14.081 --> 23:16.792
Aside from you, only one person.

484
23:18.711 --> 23:19.629
Who is it?

485
23:21.172 --> 23:23.382
-It's Mr. Yoon's-- -[knocking on door]

486
23:25.176 --> 23:26.177
Let me call you back.

487
23:37.104 --> 23:39.106
[suspenseful music continues]

488
23:40.358 --> 23:41.943
Han Eun-young, are you there?

489
23:42.026 --> 23:43.527
[phone buzzes]

490
23:44.737 --> 23:47.323
THIS IS THE PHOTO OF THE RETAINED EARNINGS LEDGER I TOOK EARLIER

491
23:52.662 --> 23:55.373
[Captain Park] We've discovered an additional phone belonging to Ms. Han,

492
23:55.456 --> 23:57.375
and you're the last one on the call logs.

493
23:57.458 --> 23:59.126
We'd like you to come in for questioning.

494
23:59.627 --> 24:00.753
Okay.

495
24:07.260 --> 24:09.762
[Ms. Han] Aside from you, only one person.

496
24:11.347 --> 24:12.556
It's Mr. Yoon's--

497
24:12.640 --> 24:15.851
Yoon Yi-jun's. His who?

498
24:17.144 --> 24:18.271
Inner circle?

499
24:20.690 --> 24:22.024
Kim Si-hyun?

500
24:25.653 --> 24:28.072
He knew a lot, but there were still some gaps.

501
24:32.785 --> 24:34.829
Whose side are you really on, Si-hyun?

502
24:40.084 --> 24:43.004
[soft, pensive music playing]

503
24:46.632 --> 24:50.011
For the first time in my life, I've been rejected.

504
24:50.094 --> 24:51.637
Do you have any old friends?

505
24:54.724 --> 24:56.392
[Si-hyun] She stabbed me in the back.

506
24:58.644 --> 24:59.562
It hurts.

507
25:01.188 --> 25:03.232
Like an older friend who you hold hands with.

508
25:03.316 --> 25:05.318
When a woman leaves, I don't stop her.

509
25:05.401 --> 25:07.236
I have finally…

510
25:08.571 --> 25:11.449
reached a definitive understanding about all this chaos.

511
25:11.532 --> 25:13.576
I view him as a cute younger sibling.

512
25:13.659 --> 25:15.619
That's why when he's insolent,

513
25:15.703 --> 25:17.997
I forgive it because I see him as a little brother.

514
25:18.080 --> 25:20.041
So why do I feel so crappy?

515
25:21.042 --> 25:22.168
I don't get it.

516
25:22.877 --> 25:25.254
Is he seriously willing to hold hands with just anyone?

517
25:25.921 --> 25:27.673
I can't stop thinking about her.

518
25:27.757 --> 25:29.633
When we were leaving the restaurant--

519
25:29.717 --> 25:31.177
[Yi-jun] Yeah, when we were leaving.

520
25:31.260 --> 25:33.012
When I was coming out of the police station.

521
25:33.095 --> 25:35.848
Yeah, when you were coming out of the police station.

522
25:35.931 --> 25:37.725
-[music deflates] -You what?

523
25:38.392 --> 25:39.393
What police station?

524
25:39.477 --> 25:41.020
-[gasps softly] -Huh?

525
25:41.103 --> 25:42.605
[playful music playing]

526
25:42.688 --> 25:43.647
Why were you there?

527
25:44.398 --> 25:45.399
Why was I there?

528
25:46.484 --> 25:47.818
[Captain Park] How many times has this happened?

529
25:48.444 --> 25:52.198
When are you finally gonna learn not to run off like that, huh?

530
25:52.281 --> 25:54.200
Bong-yi, everyone who works with him

531
25:54.283 --> 25:57.620
knows that Yi-jun's got a nasty temper and always gets what he wants.

532
25:57.703 --> 26:00.790
I actually think Kang exercised impressive self-restraint.

533
26:00.873 --> 26:01.749
Get out of the car.

534
26:01.832 --> 26:02.833
You're on your own.

535
26:04.126 --> 26:05.669
[Captain Park sighs]

536
26:06.379 --> 26:08.214
Hey, why are you getting so sloppy right now

537
26:08.297 --> 26:10.591
after you've worked so hard to get in there and find that phone?

538
26:10.674 --> 26:12.718
You're a police officer working undercover!

539
26:12.802 --> 26:16.097
As if running around in public with your target wasn't bad enough,

540
26:16.180 --> 26:17.306
you wound up arrested!

541
26:18.766 --> 26:19.767
I'm sorry, sir.

542
26:20.684 --> 26:22.061
I am telling you now,

543
26:22.144 --> 26:24.814
if this happens again, I'm taking you off the case.

544
26:26.899 --> 26:28.484
[sighs]

545
26:28.567 --> 26:30.861
[soft, pensive music playing]

546
26:33.239 --> 26:34.615
[thug shouts]

547
26:47.002 --> 26:48.421
What are you still doing here?

548
26:53.300 --> 26:54.927
Uh, thanks for this.

549
26:56.262 --> 26:57.471
Let's move on Kim Si-hyun.

550
26:59.348 --> 27:01.392
Haven't they set a date to bring in Hye-jung?

551
27:01.475 --> 27:03.978
-Shouldn't it be after that? -Same day.

552
27:05.771 --> 27:07.398
We can't afford to wait longer.

553
27:08.149 --> 27:09.316
That's true.

554
27:12.653 --> 27:14.196
I saw earlier.

555
27:15.865 --> 27:17.116
Out front.

556
27:17.199 --> 27:20.119
[tense, dramatic music playing]

557
27:25.291 --> 27:26.750
[sighs]

558
27:28.961 --> 27:31.922
-Seok-jin, that was all Yi-jun, he get-- -I believe you.

559
27:32.631 --> 27:34.091
But he shouldn't do that.

560
27:37.052 --> 27:39.180
Okay. I'm sorry.

561
27:41.557 --> 27:42.850
Let's wrap this thing up. [sighs]

562
27:57.031 --> 27:58.282
[exhales]

563
27:59.450 --> 28:03.037
All right. So a guy Kang's close with showed up at the police station,

564
28:03.120 --> 28:04.455
and now you're jealous?

565
28:04.538 --> 28:07.541
Please. You have to be mad to be jealous.

566
28:07.625 --> 28:09.168
"Why do I feel so crappy?"

567
28:09.251 --> 28:10.544
[quirky, pensive music playing]

568
28:10.628 --> 28:13.923
"Is he seriously willing to hold hands with just anyone?"

569
28:14.006 --> 28:14.924
Was that it?

570
28:16.008 --> 28:17.593
How many times do I have to tell you?

571
28:17.676 --> 28:21.722
The only reason I feel like this is 'cause he's like a little brother.

572
28:21.805 --> 28:23.974
Okay, then why do you care?

573
28:24.934 --> 28:28.521
Why can't he hold hands with some dude if he's your little brother?

574
28:31.232 --> 28:32.483
Come on, bud.

575
28:32.566 --> 28:34.485
Why does him doing that bother you?

576
28:34.568 --> 28:35.778
Are you jealous he and I get along?

577
28:35.861 --> 28:37.988
-How is that relevant? -You see?

578
28:38.072 --> 28:39.365
You're a jealous guy.

579
28:40.574 --> 28:43.202
You know, human brains are strange.

580
28:43.285 --> 28:45.704
After we consume any amount of glucose,

581
28:45.788 --> 28:48.415
it's like we start lying to ourselves about stuff.

582
28:48.499 --> 28:52.253
You can make excuses all you want. "Oh, what we have is purely platonic.

583
28:53.921 --> 28:55.339
He's like my little brother."

584
28:56.799 --> 28:58.050
-But it would just make things harder. -[gentle piano music playing]

585
28:58.801 --> 29:00.469
[quirky, pensive music continues]

586
29:01.136 --> 29:04.557
[sighs] Just making your life more difficult.

587
29:17.152 --> 29:18.237
Kim Si-hyun.

588
29:18.320 --> 29:21.407
About the milk, why is Mr. Kim the one who brings it over?

589
29:21.490 --> 29:23.200
Well, it's imported and organic.

590
29:23.284 --> 29:26.036
It's from an imported food store near Mr. Kim's house.

591
29:37.715 --> 29:40.384
[tense music playing]

592
29:42.219 --> 29:44.513
Up until yesterday, you were pretending.

593
29:44.597 --> 29:45.889
Now it's all out in the open.

594
29:47.099 --> 29:48.642
Want me to stop playing dumb?

595
29:49.893 --> 29:52.646
Fine. Let's review what we swept under the rug,

596
29:52.730 --> 29:53.897
starting with Jerry's bowl.

597
29:54.481 --> 29:55.774
Why did you hide it?

598
29:55.858 --> 29:59.945
That night, I thought you were making quite a big deal over nothing.

599
30:00.029 --> 30:02.406
[tense music playing]

600
30:02.489 --> 30:05.075
I didn't wanna waste it, so I poured him some.

601
30:05.159 --> 30:07.870
But the next day, I saw the bowl's color had changed.

602
30:11.123 --> 30:12.583
I see.

603
30:12.666 --> 30:14.918
That's why you kept stopping me whenever I picked up a glass,

604
30:15.502 --> 30:17.546
and why you were looking for signs of danger.

605
30:17.630 --> 30:20.549
That's also the reason you asked Ms. Choi about Si-hyun.

606
30:20.633 --> 30:21.842
Yes, sir.

607
30:24.136 --> 30:25.346
Ding-dong.

608
30:27.681 --> 30:28.974
Milk delivery's here.

609
30:33.103 --> 30:34.313
[music fades]

610
30:35.564 --> 30:36.982
Give it a rest.

611
30:39.360 --> 30:41.528
[uneasy music playing]

612
30:44.031 --> 30:46.450
There's only one person in the house who touches this milk.

613
30:46.533 --> 30:48.035
That person would be Mr. Yoon.

614
30:48.118 --> 30:50.204
I'm sure someone's trying to tamper with it.

615
30:50.287 --> 30:51.664
Not anyone in here,

616
30:52.581 --> 30:53.624
someone outside the house.

617
31:03.467 --> 31:04.510
[exhales]

618
31:07.930 --> 31:10.724
Could be tainted. Guess we're gonna find out.

619
31:12.226 --> 31:16.021
I wonder, Mr. Kang, why'd you decide to go rogue?

620
31:16.105 --> 31:17.898
Why didn't you just throw it away?

621
31:20.025 --> 31:21.527
Are you seriously suspecting me?

622
31:21.610 --> 31:23.362
[Si-hyun] A good secretary does exactly

623
31:23.445 --> 31:25.948
what Mr. Yoon orders them to do, no matter the order.

624
31:26.031 --> 31:27.533
I'll give an example.

625
31:28.534 --> 31:31.412
When a VIP lands himself in jail, he contacts his lawyer,

626
31:32.329 --> 31:33.747
but you stopped him.

627
31:34.123 --> 31:35.124
[sighs]

628
31:35.207 --> 31:36.667
I've noticed a trend of yours.

629
31:36.750 --> 31:38.794
You've often been ignoring your boss's orders.

630
31:40.671 --> 31:42.047
I wonder why that is.

631
31:42.798 --> 31:44.425
I made a mistake down at the police station

632
31:44.508 --> 31:45.676
during the interrogation.

633
31:45.759 --> 31:46.760
That was wrong.

634
31:47.636 --> 31:48.929
But with that bowl,

635
31:50.431 --> 31:52.516
I don't think it would've changed color

636
31:52.599 --> 31:54.727
if it were filled with any old liquid.

637
31:55.436 --> 31:57.146
[Jae-hee] Someone was trying to kill Mr. Yoon,

638
31:57.229 --> 31:59.398
and I have been hearing some interesting rumors…

639
32:00.649 --> 32:02.943
about your relationship with Yoon Na-jung.

640
32:05.654 --> 32:07.156
Okay, let's drop it.

641
32:08.240 --> 32:09.324
So he's…

642
32:10.784 --> 32:11.660
not the guy.

643
32:12.411 --> 32:15.205
Sir, why… why are you so sure about that?

644
32:17.458 --> 32:19.293
'Cause I told him to do it.

645
32:20.836 --> 32:22.629
I told him to talk to her.

646
32:22.713 --> 32:24.173
That's why they were together.

647
32:24.256 --> 32:26.884
-[whimsical music playing] -Hey, being suspected

648
32:26.967 --> 32:28.010
was kind of cool, though.

649
32:29.011 --> 32:30.596
[Si-hyun] Why'd you tell him all that?

650
32:30.679 --> 32:33.557
-Wipe the milk off your chin. -Huh? Oh, geez.

651
32:33.640 --> 32:36.351
He was keeping tabs on you 'cause you're in my inner circle.

652
32:36.435 --> 32:38.020
You understand that.

653
32:38.520 --> 32:39.730
[Yi-jun] There's no reason to suspect him.

654
32:39.813 --> 32:41.356
He is kind of weird, though.

655
32:42.441 --> 32:43.734
[Si-hyun] You've been spying on me?

656
32:43.817 --> 32:46.487
[laughs] Exciting!

657
32:46.570 --> 32:48.322
Were you all, like, behind the bushes?

658
32:49.072 --> 32:50.365
That's awesome.

659
32:52.451 --> 32:53.285
[elevator chimes]

660
32:54.077 --> 32:55.037
What? What?

661
32:55.954 --> 32:57.581
-[Hye-jung] Hi, sir, how are you? -[staff] Hello, sir.

662
32:58.665 --> 33:00.292
[Jae-hee] Let me carry that for you, missy.

663
33:03.295 --> 33:05.380
Hi, Mr. Kang. How have you been?

664
33:06.381 --> 33:08.509
So this is purely out of curiosity,

665
33:08.592 --> 33:10.093
are you dating anyone right now?

666
33:10.886 --> 33:12.513
[quirky music playing]

667
33:12.596 --> 33:13.472
Huh?

668
33:14.681 --> 33:15.557
Uh…

669
33:17.100 --> 33:17.976
Uh…

670
33:18.060 --> 33:19.436
[whispers] Remember to breathe, okay?

671
33:22.439 --> 33:24.983
Oh, sir, I need to tell you something about today's schedule.

672
33:25.818 --> 33:26.860
Uh…

673
33:27.778 --> 33:30.072
[upbeat playful music playing]

674
33:35.327 --> 33:37.538
You're into him. I can tell it's a crush.

675
33:38.747 --> 33:39.873
Wow.

676
33:39.957 --> 33:41.333
You're not even denying it.

677
33:42.417 --> 33:43.502
Having fun?

678
33:43.585 --> 33:44.503
This isn't…

679
33:45.254 --> 33:48.382
I hope you're enjoying watching me struggle with my attraction.

680
33:48.465 --> 33:50.425
Let me tell you, AI is gonna replace all human love

681
33:50.509 --> 33:52.261
after the fourth industrial revolution,

682
33:52.344 --> 33:54.513
so go love who you want, bro!

683
33:54.596 --> 33:56.098
[laughing]

684
33:56.682 --> 33:58.559
Hey, he's apparently pretty popular.

685
33:58.642 --> 34:00.394
Man, you should have seen your face.

686
34:00.477 --> 34:03.897
Anyone would be like, "Oh, God, this is heating up."

687
34:04.940 --> 34:05.858
You're one to talk.

688
34:06.441 --> 34:07.693
I've been wondering who dumped you.

689
34:07.776 --> 34:09.236
It was Ms. Lee, wasn't it?

690
34:09.319 --> 34:11.947
Your face is like a polygraph test, you know that?

691
34:12.030 --> 34:15.492
[fake crying] "I just got dumped. She broke my heart."

692
34:16.410 --> 34:20.038
Earlier, she handed him that box as soon as he offered.

693
34:20.622 --> 34:22.666
Like she ever would have done that for me.

694
34:22.749 --> 34:24.793
Why are women like that?

695
34:24.877 --> 34:26.587
Why does she like Jae-hee?

696
34:26.670 --> 34:28.797
Oh, I forgot. You're into him, too.

697
34:28.881 --> 34:30.883
[laughs]

698
34:30.966 --> 34:31.967
Get out!

699
34:32.551 --> 34:36.179
-Don't you have work? -[chuckles] Fine. I'm going.

700
34:36.263 --> 34:38.265
We do need to finish our conversation.

701
34:39.141 --> 34:40.684
I brought that milk every time.

702
34:41.518 --> 34:43.353
No matter how much I think about it,

703
34:43.729 --> 34:45.647
I have no clue how they got to it.

704
34:46.064 --> 34:47.608
-Should we tell the police about it? -[Yi-jun] We can't.

705
34:48.525 --> 34:49.651
If rumors get out,

706
34:49.735 --> 34:52.029
all the company's stock prices will go into free fall.

707
34:52.779 --> 34:54.031
-Even so-- -[phone buzzes]

708
34:57.951 --> 34:59.077
Just a sec.

709
35:01.747 --> 35:02.831
Yeah?

710
35:07.294 --> 35:08.128
I understand.

711
35:09.296 --> 35:10.297
I'll get back to you.

712
35:14.968 --> 35:15.886
Who was that?

713
35:18.138 --> 35:19.097
The police.

714
35:19.181 --> 35:21.141
They just found Ms. Han's phone.

715
35:21.892 --> 35:23.727
They're setting up a date for questioning.

716
35:25.562 --> 35:26.521
Oh.

717
35:26.605 --> 35:29.608
[pensive, tense music swells]

718
35:31.610 --> 35:32.819
[music fades]

719
35:33.028 --> 35:35.280
-[Hye-jung] Mr. Kang. -Yes?

720
35:36.573 --> 35:37.699
Thank you for helping out.

721
35:37.783 --> 35:38.867
Oh, don't mention it.

722
35:39.785 --> 35:43.121
Would you mind checking in on Mr. Yoon's weekend schedule?

723
35:44.498 --> 35:45.832
I'm asking because

724
35:45.916 --> 35:48.168
the chairman's requested a dinner with you and Lee Si-a.

725
35:49.294 --> 35:50.295
Oh.

726
35:50.754 --> 35:51.838
Right. I'll do that.

727
35:53.298 --> 35:54.841
By the way, Ms. Lee,

728
35:54.925 --> 35:57.844
can I ask, were you close to his former secretary?

729
35:58.595 --> 35:59.846
Was I close with Ms. Han?

730
36:00.097 --> 36:03.100
[tense dramatic music playing]

731
36:03.517 --> 36:04.726
We started here together.

732
36:05.852 --> 36:07.062
Why are you asking?

733
36:07.604 --> 36:10.607
Oh, Mr. Jung had mentioned the two of you were very close.

734
36:11.274 --> 36:13.068
He said you looked after her.

735
36:13.819 --> 36:14.945
You must be devastated.

736
36:19.533 --> 36:22.202
[tense musical sting]

737
36:31.294 --> 36:34.214
[tense dramatic music continues]

738
36:43.890 --> 36:44.975
Lee Hye-jung.

739
36:51.189 --> 36:54.067
That's just as a witness. We don't know anything yet.

740
36:54.151 --> 36:55.485
Hmm.

741
36:58.030 --> 37:00.115
I let myself be distracted at a critical time.

742
37:01.950 --> 37:03.493
Whatever. Forget it.

743
37:04.119 --> 37:05.829
None of it made any sense anyhow.

744
37:08.081 --> 37:10.625
How did I let my emotions take over?

745
37:11.960 --> 37:13.378
Keep bringing the milk.

746
37:13.462 --> 37:15.756
Stopping now will look suspicious.

747
37:15.839 --> 37:17.758
-And as for Ms. Lee-- -I'll look into it.

748
37:19.051 --> 37:21.053
[tense dramatic music swells]

749
37:22.721 --> 37:23.930
[music fades]

750
37:26.266 --> 37:28.226
-[knocking on door] -[door opens]

751
37:30.937 --> 37:32.189
[door closes]

752
37:35.192 --> 37:38.403
Sir, I have a message from the chairman's secretary.

753
37:38.487 --> 37:41.990
When would you be available for dinner with Ms. Lee this weekend?

754
37:42.074 --> 37:43.450
Seventeenth in the afternoon.

755
37:43.533 --> 37:45.994
I'll go with Mr. Jung. Don't come in that day.

756
37:46.203 --> 37:47.996
No, sir, let me join you.

757
37:50.290 --> 37:51.750
I told you about the milk bowl

758
37:51.833 --> 37:53.877
because I wanted you to be more vigilant.

759
37:54.669 --> 37:56.546
We still don't know who did it. It's dangerous.

760
37:56.630 --> 37:59.257
I know that the point of your job is to keep me safe.

761
37:59.341 --> 38:00.467
I get it.

762
38:00.550 --> 38:04.429
But I don't recall giving you permission to ignore my orders.

763
38:08.016 --> 38:08.975
Don't follow me.

764
38:09.059 --> 38:10.018
-[door opens] -[sighs]

765
38:11.228 --> 38:13.188
-[door closes] -[inhales deeply]

766
38:14.439 --> 38:16.316
[annoyed exhale] Why is he acting like this?

767
38:17.359 --> 38:19.611
Hey Mom, is Uncle getting married?

768
38:20.153 --> 38:21.363
Si-a friend's in Korea.

769
38:22.489 --> 38:23.657
Si-a's friend?

770
38:23.740 --> 38:27.577
The wedding announcement, the shareholder meeting, and the election…

771
38:28.161 --> 38:29.788
[scoffs] The timing's perfect.

772
38:30.580 --> 38:33.208
Honestly, though, I feel kind of bad for my uncle.

773
38:33.291 --> 38:36.837
His marriage, his job, there's not a thing he gets to pick for himself.

774
38:37.629 --> 38:41.299
Hmm. I wonder if he's ever truly been in love.

775
38:42.384 --> 38:43.426
[chuckles softly]

776
38:51.685 --> 38:54.563
Think of it as a pre-wedding family meal, and don't be late.

777
38:55.313 --> 38:57.315
[tense, rhythmic music playing]

778
38:58.608 --> 39:00.861
I thought we still had a little time left.

779
39:01.903 --> 39:04.614
You'll win it. You'll be the next president.

780
39:04.698 --> 39:06.950
Announce your marriage before the meeting.

781
39:08.535 --> 39:11.079
And as for the share transfer…

782
39:13.373 --> 39:14.291
get things moving.

783
39:14.916 --> 39:16.001
On it, sir.

784
39:20.505 --> 39:23.341
You're taking him up on it? You're marrying her?

785
39:23.425 --> 39:26.511
He's offering to officially hand over the reins, so I should.

786
39:27.846 --> 39:30.807
That way, whoever's after me will be forced to act now.

787
39:31.850 --> 39:33.143
[Yi-jun] And my sister?

788
39:33.226 --> 39:35.187
She was aware that Park Min-hwan

789
39:35.270 --> 39:37.314
had been digging into the retained earnings ledger.

790
39:37.397 --> 39:39.107
The fact that she was aware

791
39:39.191 --> 39:41.735
and smuggling it herself are two different things.

792
39:43.069 --> 39:45.030
-How's she doing? -[chuckles]

793
39:46.656 --> 39:49.201
She said to bring Mr. Park, and then she'll talk.

794
39:49.284 --> 39:50.619
[sighs]

795
39:52.162 --> 39:54.414
[tense music playing]

796
40:06.593 --> 40:08.595
[Si-hyun] How do you think things might have played out

797
40:09.930 --> 40:13.391
if you'd started digging into this after inheriting the company?

798
40:13.475 --> 40:15.185
Would there have been less risk?

799
40:15.268 --> 40:18.188
No. They failed on two fronts.

800
40:20.398 --> 40:22.901
The slush fund and the company.

801
40:23.985 --> 40:26.154
The money they smuggled out was merely a tool.

802
40:26.238 --> 40:27.822
Then what was their goal?

803
40:27.906 --> 40:29.324
Preventing me from taking control.

804
40:29.407 --> 40:32.118
Oh, so scary.

805
40:32.202 --> 40:33.536
[exclaims softly]

806
40:33.620 --> 40:35.121
Taekang, so scary.

807
40:35.914 --> 40:38.625
[Na-jung] Okay, blah, blah, blah, I've seen all this.

808
40:38.750 --> 40:40.418
I wonder what people are saying.

809
40:48.009 --> 40:50.929
"Yoon Na-jung loves to lord her power over everyone."

810
40:51.012 --> 40:52.764
SMOKING IN A NO SMOKING AREA

811
40:52.847 --> 40:54.182
SHE'S SO INSUFFERABLE

812
40:54.266 --> 40:56.935
They've got nothing better to do than write this?

813
40:59.479 --> 41:00.480
[sighs]

814
41:01.982 --> 41:04.359
MEET AT SIX USUAL SPOT

815
41:04.442 --> 41:06.361
[menacing music playing]

816
41:20.333 --> 41:23.670
Up until now, Mr. Kim's been hiding it well.

817
41:23.753 --> 41:26.756
Interesting. Anything else?

818
41:26.840 --> 41:28.758
I don't know if it's 'cause he was caught,

819
41:28.842 --> 41:32.262
but he was asked to drink the milk, so he did.

820
41:33.346 --> 41:37.267
And then Mr. Yoon, well… [sighs]

821
41:38.935 --> 41:41.521
-Ms. Choi, listen. -Yes?

822
41:43.857 --> 41:45.025
I'll be the judge here.

823
41:45.108 --> 41:46.985
Oh, right.

824
41:47.068 --> 41:49.863
So stop omitting things and just tell me what you know.

825
41:49.946 --> 41:53.074
You've had no issues taking my cash up till now, isn't that right?

826
41:53.158 --> 41:54.451
[whimpers]

827
41:55.035 --> 41:56.244
I know this much,

828
41:56.328 --> 41:57.537
Mr. Yoon trusts Kang.

829
41:57.620 --> 42:00.248
I heard him defend him to Mr. Kim earlier.

830
42:02.584 --> 42:04.169
-There's actually someone he trusts? -Mm-hmm.

831
42:04.252 --> 42:06.254
[menacing music continues]

832
42:07.130 --> 42:08.173
That Mr. Kang…

833
42:08.757 --> 42:09.924
What about him?

834
42:10.008 --> 42:11.676
Make sure you keep an eye on him.

835
42:12.344 --> 42:13.595
Oh, right.

836
42:14.804 --> 42:17.057
[menacing music swells]

837
42:19.851 --> 42:20.852
[music fades]

838
42:21.978 --> 42:23.188
[sighs]

839
42:23.855 --> 42:26.816
I always thought that guy was such a sneaky weirdo.

840
42:26.900 --> 42:29.402
I was certain he was working with Yoon Na-jung.

841
42:29.486 --> 42:31.363
And if Si-hyun wasn't the one who did it,

842
42:32.072 --> 42:34.199
who the heck laced the milk then?

843
42:38.745 --> 42:39.579
Hey, Kang!

844
42:39.954 --> 42:41.956
[quirky music playing]

845
42:42.040 --> 42:44.501
You remember what the captain used to tell us?

846
42:44.584 --> 42:46.002
Gotta start from scratch.

847
42:47.295 --> 42:48.797
I don't know.

848
42:49.422 --> 42:50.382
Oh!

849
42:55.804 --> 42:57.138
You're not looking great.

850
42:58.056 --> 42:59.849
You look like a weed that's been pulled out of the ground.

851
42:59.933 --> 43:01.601
Yi-jun chew you out again?

852
43:02.394 --> 43:03.812
It's not like he does that every day.

853
43:04.771 --> 43:06.439
He's not such a bad guy, you know?

854
43:07.774 --> 43:09.150
What'd you just say?

855
43:09.234 --> 43:10.735
You're defending him now?

856
43:17.242 --> 43:19.244
[soft, uneasy music playing]

857
43:33.049 --> 43:34.342
Don't come inside. Just leave.

858
43:35.051 --> 43:36.511
Let me just check on the security.

859
43:36.594 --> 43:38.471
We talked about doing as you're told.

860
43:41.099 --> 43:42.100
I'll admit.

861
43:42.725 --> 43:46.980
Maybe I've been too soft on you, lenient, though it's not just you, actually.

862
43:47.063 --> 43:49.858
I've been less bitchy toward other people, too.

863
43:50.775 --> 43:54.070
Wanna guess what happened because of that attitude change?

864
43:56.531 --> 43:58.324
They took advantage of my kindness

865
43:59.784 --> 44:01.035
and forgot their place.

866
44:05.457 --> 44:06.958
[sighs]

867
44:07.041 --> 44:09.461
He goes from burning hot to ice cold,

868
44:09.544 --> 44:12.172
slightly less bitchy to incredibly bitchy!

869
44:12.839 --> 44:14.340
It's like he's trying to drive me insane.

870
44:15.508 --> 44:17.552
Oh, hang on, you called me your brother.

871
44:17.635 --> 44:19.179
You're the one who kissed… [breathing shakily]

872
44:19.929 --> 44:21.139
[exhales softly]

873
44:21.222 --> 44:23.141
Oh, my God.

874
44:23.391 --> 44:24.809
[phone buzzes]

875
44:27.270 --> 44:28.229
Who is this?

876
44:32.901 --> 44:34.944
[soft jazz ambient music playing]

877
44:40.825 --> 44:41.910
[sighs worriedly]

878
44:51.461 --> 44:54.339
You had something you wanted to tell me about my boss?

879
44:54.422 --> 44:55.381
Actually…

880
44:56.299 --> 44:59.219
I have this funny little thing where I can't stop lying.

881
45:00.220 --> 45:01.804
I was afraid that you wouldn't come.

882
45:01.888 --> 45:05.475
You sure are dressed fairly reserved for someone who loves to lie.

883
45:06.434 --> 45:07.936
This isn't working, is it?

884
45:08.019 --> 45:09.521
Ugh, I knew it looked off.

885
45:10.480 --> 45:11.356
I'll be right back.

886
45:11.731 --> 45:13.858
Ugh, what am I even doing here?

887
45:13.983 --> 45:17.737
[mystical, rhythmic music playing]

888
45:23.201 --> 45:24.452
[gasps]

889
45:24.536 --> 45:27.956
If I'm gonna go up against the chairman, I better be wearing something like this.

890
45:28.748 --> 45:30.166
I'll wear it to the pre-wedding dinner.

891
45:30.250 --> 45:32.043
Oh, is that what this dinner is for?

892
45:32.126 --> 45:34.796
[scoffs] They're pretending it's just dinner,

893
45:34.879 --> 45:37.131
but we all know they're setting the date while we're all there.

894
45:41.135 --> 45:42.470
Why?

895
45:43.054 --> 45:44.055
You don't like this one?

896
45:44.138 --> 45:46.015
Okay. Change.

897
45:46.099 --> 45:48.476
Uh, no. I think that's the prettiest. It is!

898
45:50.144 --> 45:53.147
[gentle, charming music playing]

899
46:14.419 --> 46:15.628
[Si-a giggling]

900
46:16.921 --> 46:17.964
[inaudible]

901
46:23.177 --> 46:24.887
[chuckles]

902
46:25.805 --> 46:27.265
[chuckles]

903
46:30.018 --> 46:31.269
[Si-a sighs softly]

904
46:33.813 --> 46:35.273
[Si-a] Mr. Kang.

905
46:36.274 --> 46:37.400
Can you hear me?

906
46:37.483 --> 46:38.484
[music stops]

907
46:44.782 --> 46:45.783
You're beautiful.

908
46:45.867 --> 46:47.368
[chuckles softly]

909
46:47.994 --> 46:50.204
SEOUL METROPOLITAN POLICE AGENCY

910
46:50.288 --> 46:53.291
MOBILE PHONE FORENSIC EXAMINATION REPORT

911
46:53.374 --> 46:54.834
[tense, investigative music playing]

912
47:01.883 --> 47:04.260
We've recovered the data wiped from Han Eun-young's phone.

913
47:04.344 --> 47:07.513
If your testimony contradicts the data, that'll be used against you.

914
47:09.432 --> 47:10.725
[camera chimes]

915
47:12.894 --> 47:14.062
Let's begin.

916
47:14.145 --> 47:15.772
You are Lee Hye-jung, correct?

917
47:19.776 --> 47:21.486
-[clears throat] -[Seok-jin] Superintendent.

918
47:23.655 --> 47:24.572
[superior] Come on in.

919
47:24.656 --> 47:27.116
[tense, investigative music rises]

920
47:30.536 --> 47:32.580
[tense, investigative music continues]

921
47:34.999 --> 47:36.417
Yes.

922
47:37.126 --> 47:38.252
The questioning's started.

923
47:39.295 --> 47:42.465
The thing is, a lawyer from Taekang's legal team

924
47:42.548 --> 47:44.133
suddenly showed up at the station.

925
47:46.344 --> 47:47.387
Kim Si-hyun.

926
47:49.347 --> 47:51.140
Ah…

927
47:52.350 --> 47:55.311
I wanted to treat my shopping buddy to a barbecue meal,

928
47:55.395 --> 47:57.063
but that will have to wait.

929
47:57.146 --> 48:00.316
There were not that many good barbecue restaurant options anyway.

930
48:00.400 --> 48:01.359
Hmm.

931
48:01.693 --> 48:02.819
I just needed it,

932
48:02.902 --> 48:04.529
I have an uncomfortable dinner coming up, so…

933
48:04.612 --> 48:06.489
I think I've made it very clear.

934
48:06.572 --> 48:08.408
I have no intention of sharing a meal with you.

935
48:08.491 --> 48:10.743
The bread here is so good. Eat as much as you want.

936
48:11.869 --> 48:14.122
You know, I never said I wanted to be friends.

937
48:14.205 --> 48:16.666
If you don't have anything to tell me about Mr. Yoon,

938
48:16.749 --> 48:17.875
I'd better be leaving.

939
48:18.501 --> 48:19.502
[sighs]

940
48:19.585 --> 48:21.546
I actually know quite a lot about Yi-jun.

941
48:22.755 --> 48:24.757
I mean, we go way back.

942
48:26.384 --> 48:27.427
[Si-a hums approvingly]

943
48:34.517 --> 48:37.520
We belonged to a social club for children from affluent families,

944
48:37.937 --> 48:39.439
and we went to the same school.

945
48:40.606 --> 48:41.774
THE 32ND GRADUATION CEREMONY GYEONGSEON HIGH SCHOOL

946
48:42.358 --> 48:44.402
[gentle music playing]

947
48:44.485 --> 48:46.362
[indistinct chatter]

948
48:53.119 --> 48:54.287
Congratulations.

949
48:57.790 --> 48:58.791
We're so proud of you.

950
48:58.875 --> 48:59.792
[laughs]

951
48:59.876 --> 49:01.753
-[student] One, two, three. -[camera shutter clicks]

952
49:01.836 --> 49:04.088
-Thank you. [chuckles] -Oh, that's so nice. So proud of you.

953
49:04.172 --> 49:06.132
[Si-a] He's been like this ever since he was a kid.

954
49:07.467 --> 49:11.304
Even though he had a chauffeured sedan to come pick him up at the entrance,

955
49:13.306 --> 49:16.768
he envied the kids whose mothers came to get them in person.

956
49:17.935 --> 49:20.772
And even though a chef packed him a meal with 30 different banchan

957
49:20.855 --> 49:22.690
whenever there was a school picnic,

958
49:23.399 --> 49:25.151
he wanted the other kids' gimbap.

959
49:26.611 --> 49:27.612
He had this hunger,

960
49:28.196 --> 49:32.241
the kind of hunger you only feel as a kid who's never had that.

961
49:34.619 --> 49:36.537
Even though he could literally buy anything,

962
49:36.621 --> 49:38.790
he only wants the things that money can't buy.

963
49:39.457 --> 49:41.042
He instinctively knows what they are,

964
49:41.125 --> 49:43.503
the things he can't buy no matter how hard he tries.

965
49:46.339 --> 49:48.174
I don't know why you're telling me all this.

966
49:49.091 --> 49:51.093
I doubt Mr. Yoon would appreciate it.

967
49:51.177 --> 49:53.429
I wanna give him something he can't purchase.

968
49:54.722 --> 49:57.642
The thing is, I like him a lot.

969
50:03.981 --> 50:08.361
Honestly, the whole reason I'm getting married is to be happier.

970
50:09.946 --> 50:11.906
He should experience that, too.

971
50:14.992 --> 50:16.327
[music fades]

972
50:18.955 --> 50:19.872
[Si-a] You made it.

973
50:20.623 --> 50:24.043
Isn't this what you wanted? You were trying to get me to come.

974
50:31.342 --> 50:32.969
Why'd you meet up with her?

975
50:33.052 --> 50:35.221
Why do you insist on doing whatever you want?

976
50:35.763 --> 50:38.599
You were the one who told me to give her my number.

977
50:38.683 --> 50:41.018
That didn't mean you could meet up in private.

978
50:41.102 --> 50:43.145
Do you think I wanted to come here?

979
50:43.229 --> 50:45.314
She said she had something really important to tell me about you.

980
50:45.398 --> 50:46.649
How could I possibly ignore that?

981
50:46.732 --> 50:48.985
I don't think you wanted to ignore her.

982
50:50.152 --> 50:51.779
You two were having a good time, right?

983
50:51.863 --> 50:53.155
Don't put words in my mouth.

984
50:53.239 --> 50:55.157
If you wanna be my secretary, act like it.

985
50:55.741 --> 50:57.910
Seeing Si-a behind my back for a shopping date…

986
50:57.994 --> 51:00.121
that's not in the job description.

987
51:00.204 --> 51:02.665
Then let me do the job I was hired to do.

988
51:02.748 --> 51:04.208
Your life's obviously in danger,

989
51:04.292 --> 51:05.918
but you keep insisting on putting a wall between us.

990
51:06.002 --> 51:07.628
Just follow the damn orders!

991
51:08.296 --> 51:11.257
If I tell you not to come, don't, and if I say to leave, then go.

992
51:12.133 --> 51:15.011
If I'm not even allowed to talk to someone who knows you so well,

993
51:15.803 --> 51:17.179
how am I supposed to do this?

994
51:20.057 --> 51:20.975
Forget it.

995
51:22.101 --> 51:24.312
If you're gonna keep doing whatever you want,

996
51:24.729 --> 51:25.563
then go.

997
51:25.646 --> 51:26.898
Just get out.

998
51:27.815 --> 51:30.067
Yeah. I'll go.

999
51:31.485 --> 51:32.945
I'm officially quitting.

1000
51:34.447 --> 51:36.032
You're such a…

1001
51:37.617 --> 51:39.952
-[breathes deeply] -[somber piano music playing]

1002
51:40.036 --> 51:41.746
[Jae-hee] I guess I was wrong about you.

1003
51:47.376 --> 51:49.295
I thought you were a good person after all.

1004
52:03.351 --> 52:04.602
-[music fades] -[crickets chirping]

1005
52:04.685 --> 52:07.521
I imagine you'll be quite busy with the upcoming elections.

1006
52:07.772 --> 52:08.940
[chuckles]

1007
52:09.482 --> 52:12.234
What could upstage the most important day of my daughter's life?

1008
52:13.069 --> 52:15.321
These two have been engaged for a long time.

1009
52:15.404 --> 52:18.115
Let's not delay further. What are your thoughts?

1010
52:23.329 --> 52:24.830
I'll do whatever Si-a wants.

1011
52:26.123 --> 52:27.208
Hmm.

1012
52:28.084 --> 52:31.712
Chairman, there's a certain wedding gift my heart's set on.

1013
52:32.296 --> 52:34.090
[Tae-sik] You want me to hand over Taekang?

1014
52:34.173 --> 52:35.091
[Si-a chuckles]

1015
52:35.174 --> 52:38.427
I wouldn't say no if you offered it, but it's something else.

1016
52:40.680 --> 52:41.639
Kang Jae-hee.

1017
52:42.682 --> 52:45.476
He was recently hired as Yi-jun's personal secretary.

1018
52:46.018 --> 52:47.269
He's so good at his work.

1019
52:48.938 --> 52:50.106
That's what I want.

1020
52:50.898 --> 52:53.901
[unsettling music playing]

1021
52:58.114 --> 53:00.199
[Jae-hee's dad] As my buddy Shakespeare once said,

1022
53:00.992 --> 53:03.411
"If thou rememb'rest not the slightest folly

1023
53:03.494 --> 53:05.162
that love did make thee run into.

1024
53:05.246 --> 53:07.873
That means thou hast not loved."

1025
53:07.957 --> 53:10.918
I get it. What on earth is he saying?

1026
53:11.002 --> 53:12.044
Yeah, good question.

1027
53:12.128 --> 53:15.965
Whether you're a king, chaebol kid, beggar even,

1028
53:16.048 --> 53:18.467
everyone makes mistakes.

1029
53:19.218 --> 53:20.594
Love makes everyone a fool.

1030
53:21.178 --> 53:23.389
Everybody. [chuckles]

1031
53:23.472 --> 53:25.391
Yeah, you'd know all about that.

1032
53:25.474 --> 53:27.435
I told you not to interrupt me while I'm doing this.

1033
53:27.518 --> 53:28.769
What the hell's wrong with you?

1034
53:30.104 --> 53:32.189
Get off your foolish little butt and go see Jae-hee.

1035
53:32.273 --> 53:34.358
Do it before I give you a smack.

1036
53:35.067 --> 53:37.528
Tomorrow's the day. You need to hurry up and get ready.

1037
53:37.611 --> 53:39.030
It's really been a year?

1038
53:40.072 --> 53:42.158
[riders scream excitedly]

1039
53:45.369 --> 53:47.329
[cheerful music playing]

1040
54:00.468 --> 54:01.761
Hello, nice to meet you.

1041
54:04.305 --> 54:05.347
Oh, hey, Papa!

1042
54:05.431 --> 54:07.892
-Papa! -[Jae-hee] There's my boy!

1043
54:07.975 --> 54:09.602
-Papa! -[grunts]

1044
54:10.102 --> 54:11.604
-You doing good? -Uh-huh.

1045
54:11.687 --> 54:14.023
-Great. Ready to go have some fun? -Uh-huh.

1046
54:14.106 --> 54:16.025
-Let's go! -Let's go!

1047
54:16.609 --> 54:17.526
[man] Hit the black!

1048
54:18.736 --> 54:20.112
[laughs]

1049
54:20.196 --> 54:22.865
Yay, you're the best, Papa!

1050
54:24.158 --> 54:25.201
Uh… Oh, great.

1051
54:26.452 --> 54:29.622
[kid] You were the number one marksman in the army, right, Papa?

1052
54:29.705 --> 54:32.583
Of course, I hit every target right in the middle.

1053
54:33.084 --> 54:34.585
-Hi. -[teasingly] Nana-nana-na na!

1054
54:36.462 --> 54:38.756
-Honey? Here. -[man] Yeah, right there, buddy. Yeah.

1055
54:38.839 --> 54:40.132
What's wrong?

1056
54:40.216 --> 54:41.342
-Papa. -Uh-huh.

1057
54:45.471 --> 54:47.681
That guy takes this way too serious.

1058
54:48.808 --> 54:50.184
[sighs]

1059
54:51.102 --> 54:52.728
-Let's show these guys. -Uh-huh.

1060
54:52.812 --> 54:53.687
[Jae-hee] Let's go.

1061
54:55.189 --> 54:56.857
[grunts]

1062
54:57.691 --> 54:58.734
Fix your posture.

1063
54:58.818 --> 55:00.194
[air rifle firing]

1064
55:00.277 --> 55:02.071
-Five points! -[audience] Whoa.

1065
55:02.154 --> 55:03.739
[staff] Five points.

1066
55:04.532 --> 55:05.366
Five again!

1067
55:05.449 --> 55:06.575
That was perfect!

1068
55:06.659 --> 55:07.952
[applauding]

1069
55:08.035 --> 55:11.163
[bright, upbeat music playing]

1070
55:12.331 --> 55:13.749
-See that? -Uh-huh.

1071
55:13.833 --> 55:16.877
Buddy, in the army I used to shoot real guns, you know that.

1072
55:16.961 --> 55:18.129
That's way harder than this.

1073
55:18.212 --> 55:20.214
Anyone can shoot these things. [chuckles]

1074
55:20.297 --> 55:22.341
Are you also in the Special Forces now?

1075
55:22.424 --> 55:23.592
Hmm?

1076
55:23.676 --> 55:26.178
I asked you, are you also in the Special Forces?

1077
55:26.262 --> 55:27.513
[man] Uh…

1078
55:28.180 --> 55:29.431
Papa.

1079
55:29.515 --> 55:30.516
-Hmm? -What's Special Forces?

1080
55:30.599 --> 55:32.518
It's not better than the army, is it?

1081
55:32.601 --> 55:33.477
-[man] Mm. -[kid] Is it?

1082
55:33.561 --> 55:36.564
You know what? Why don't we go get some churros, huh?

1083
55:36.647 --> 55:38.065
[staff] You're the top scorer for the day.

1084
55:38.649 --> 55:39.775
-[Jae-hee] Oh, wow. -[staff] Congratulations, sir.

1085
55:39.859 --> 55:41.277
-Thank you. -[applauding]

1086
55:41.402 --> 55:43.863
Honey, there's binoculars and a walkie-talkie.

1087
55:43.946 --> 55:45.197
Whoa.

1088
55:46.323 --> 55:47.533
How was I?

1089
55:47.616 --> 55:48.784
You're the best.

1090
55:48.868 --> 55:49.994
Give me high five!

1091
55:50.077 --> 55:51.328
-Yeah! -Yeah!

1092
55:51.412 --> 55:53.122
[giggles]

1093
55:53.205 --> 55:54.248
[music ends]

1094
55:55.457 --> 55:57.459
[papers rustling]

1095
56:00.963 --> 56:02.256
[sighs]

1096
56:10.764 --> 56:11.932
[sighs]

1097
56:13.184 --> 56:14.560
[doorbell ringing]

1098
56:18.022 --> 56:22.067
[playful music playing]

1099
56:25.487 --> 56:26.488
Are you kidding?

1100
56:27.072 --> 56:28.073
[music ends]

1101
56:28.657 --> 56:30.284
I'm incredibly disappointed.

1102
56:31.243 --> 56:32.369
Huh?

1103
56:34.705 --> 56:37.708
It's warm outside. Hot coffee?

1104
56:38.292 --> 56:39.210
Oh, uh, right.

1105
56:40.211 --> 56:42.129
I'll take that. I'll bring an iced one.

1106
56:42.213 --> 56:44.006
[Ms. Choi chuckles awkwardly]

1107
56:44.089 --> 56:46.175
Thank you. Thank you.

1108
56:46.258 --> 56:47.843
[whimsical music playing]

1109
56:47.927 --> 56:49.136
[Si-a sighs]

1110
56:50.554 --> 56:51.472
Hmm.

1111
56:53.641 --> 56:55.351
Is Mr. Kang not here?

1112
56:55.976 --> 56:59.104
I thought today was his last workday, but he's not here.

1113
57:00.147 --> 57:01.774
-Huh. -What are you doing?

1114
57:04.860 --> 57:07.529
Well, I'm here to recruit Mr. Kang.

1115
57:07.613 --> 57:10.699
What do you think you're doing? I told you I'd play along.

1116
57:11.492 --> 57:12.493
Hm.

1117
57:13.535 --> 57:14.662
-[Jae-hee] There, over there, look! -[child] Whoa, whoa, whoa!

1118
57:14.745 --> 57:16.580
-Whoa! A lion! -Ooh!

1119
57:16.664 --> 57:18.249
[child] Wow, it's a lion.

1120
57:18.832 --> 57:20.376
-[both roaring] -[bright music playing]

1121
57:20.459 --> 57:22.628
-Its head's enormous. -That's a king bear.

1122
57:22.711 --> 57:24.713
[Jae-hee] A king bear!

1123
57:24.797 --> 57:26.966
-Its head's this small. -Its head is giant!

1124
57:27.049 --> 57:28.259
[indistinct chatter]

1125
57:31.053 --> 57:32.680
Look, the bear is standing!

1126
57:32.763 --> 57:35.015
-[Jae-hee] Say, "Roar!" -[child roaring]

1127
57:37.351 --> 57:39.353
[riders shriek excitedly]

1128
57:40.145 --> 57:42.731
[water splashing]

1129
57:43.857 --> 57:46.443
[Jae-hee] Whoa, buddy! That's a fierce face you're making!

1130
57:46.527 --> 57:48.612
Let's go again, Papa.

1131
57:48.696 --> 57:49.905
-Again? -Mm-hmm.

1132
57:49.989 --> 57:51.991
Ready? [chuckles]

1133
57:52.074 --> 57:53.784
-Okay, let's go. -[phone buzzes]

1134
57:53.867 --> 57:56.370
Oh, hold on a sec, wait, wait, hold on.

1135
57:56.453 --> 57:58.038
DO NOT ANSWER

1136
57:58.122 --> 58:00.124
[light pop music playing over speakers]

1137
58:00.207 --> 58:01.250
Hey.

1138
58:02.710 --> 58:04.128
I can't talk for very long.

1139
58:04.211 --> 58:07.172
Oh, okay. Jae-hee, an amusement park?

1140
58:07.756 --> 58:10.092
Wow, Fantasy Land!

1141
58:11.677 --> 58:12.845
Oh…

1142
58:13.762 --> 58:15.973
You're on a date right now.

1143
58:16.473 --> 58:18.309
Oh, sorry, sorry.

1144
58:18.392 --> 58:20.936
Oh, I get it, you have to go. So, I'll make this super quick.

1145
58:21.020 --> 58:23.647
I'll double your salary and triple your bonus.

1146
58:24.606 --> 58:25.524
That sound good?

1147
58:26.108 --> 58:27.526
[squeals] Wonderful.

1148
58:27.609 --> 58:30.821
Okay, you'll start at the art center next week then. Oh.

1149
58:30.904 --> 58:32.323
Have you gone crazy?

1150
58:33.073 --> 58:34.199
[panting] He…

1151
58:34.992 --> 58:36.201
Aw, he hung up.

1152
58:41.623 --> 58:42.458
SPECIAL FORCES

1153
58:42.541 --> 58:44.001
[phone chirps, line rings]

1154
58:46.420 --> 58:47.671
[Si-a] He's not picking up?

1155
58:47.880 --> 58:50.758
[sighs] I guess he has no reason to take your calls

1156
58:50.841 --> 58:52.176
now that he belongs to me.

1157
58:52.259 --> 58:54.511
You think he's an object, a thing you can throw around?

1158
58:56.680 --> 58:58.474
[sighs] This damn phone.

1159
59:02.770 --> 59:04.438
He really just agreed to all that?

1160
59:04.521 --> 59:05.481
Mm-hmm.

1161
59:07.441 --> 59:08.776
Can't you just admit it?

1162
59:11.362 --> 59:13.155
You're worried I'll steal him.

1163
59:13.238 --> 59:14.782
He's not a toy you can play with.

1164
59:15.324 --> 59:16.742
You need to leave him alone.

1165
59:17.326 --> 59:18.577
You obviously have a crush on him.

1166
59:20.120 --> 59:21.121
I can tell.

1167
59:21.747 --> 59:24.166
[gentle music playing]

1168
59:31.423 --> 59:32.758
[Si-hyun] I can tell it's a crush.

1169
59:33.550 --> 59:35.969
[Si-a] I know you like him, oppa.

1170
59:36.512 --> 59:37.471
You like Kang Jae-hee.

1171
59:39.640 --> 59:42.226
[car engine revs]

1172
59:44.186 --> 59:47.231
[upbeat festive music playing]

1173
59:58.492 --> 59:59.993
Can you see, Jin-hyung?

1174
01:00:00.077 --> 01:00:01.078
Let's see…

1175
01:00:02.204 --> 01:00:03.664
-[Jae-hee grunts] -[Jin-hyung] Wow.

1176
01:00:03.747 --> 01:00:05.999
-Wow. -Whoa.

1177
01:00:07.709 --> 01:00:09.128
[Jae-hee grunts softly]

1178
01:00:09.253 --> 01:00:11.964
-Honey, it's fun, right? -I don't know.

1179
01:00:12.047 --> 01:00:14.550
-Huh? -I know that all these dancers

1180
01:00:14.633 --> 01:00:15.926
are getting paid to do this,

1181
01:00:16.009 --> 01:00:18.846
and if I don't look happy, they won't wanna work.

1182
01:00:19.638 --> 01:00:21.640
[upbeat festive music continues]

1183
01:00:25.310 --> 01:00:26.562
Jin-hyung,

1184
01:00:26.645 --> 01:00:29.356
-why don't we find a better spot to watch? -Yeah.

1185
01:00:29.440 --> 01:00:30.607
Whoa, hey, look.

1186
01:00:30.691 --> 01:00:33.610
-[staff] There you go. -Baby, look! Look at that!

1187
01:00:33.694 --> 01:00:34.570
-Wow. -It's a balloon.

1188
01:00:34.653 --> 01:00:35.487
Hi, welcome.

1189
01:00:35.571 --> 01:00:36.655
-Thank you, sir. -Thank you, sir.

1190
01:00:36.738 --> 01:00:38.657
Yeah. Wow.

1191
01:00:38.740 --> 01:00:40.868
[upbeat festive music continues]

1192
01:00:49.877 --> 01:00:51.003
I'm onto you.

1193
01:00:51.628 --> 01:00:53.130
I can tell when you're starting to have fun.

1194
01:00:53.922 --> 01:00:56.800
No, I'm still not having that much fun.

1195
01:00:56.884 --> 01:00:58.427
Are you thinking about your mom, honey?

1196
01:00:58.510 --> 01:00:59.511
Uh…

1197
01:01:01.555 --> 01:01:04.683
Listen, your mom would want you to have so much fun

1198
01:01:04.766 --> 01:01:06.143
while you're watching all this.

1199
01:01:06.810 --> 01:01:10.689
Jin-hyung, don't lie and say you're not having fun when I know you are.

1200
01:01:11.356 --> 01:01:14.109
Let's not hold back at all, so do what you want.

1201
01:01:14.651 --> 01:01:15.861
I know.

1202
01:01:15.944 --> 01:01:20.199
I didn't know that when I was six, and now that I'm seven, I get it.

1203
01:01:20.282 --> 01:01:24.119
When I tell my mom how I really feel, she gets super sad,

1204
01:01:24.203 --> 01:01:27.748
and whenever I tell her how I miss Papa, she's sad.

1205
01:01:28.332 --> 01:01:33.253
You know, if you keep lying, you're gonna have to go to jail.

1206
01:01:33.337 --> 01:01:35.672
Honey, Papa's gonna arrest you!

1207
01:01:36.673 --> 01:01:39.551
Papa, have you never, ever told a lie before?

1208
01:01:39.635 --> 01:01:41.053
Never, ever?

1209
01:01:45.682 --> 01:01:47.434
[fireworks exploding]

1210
01:01:47.518 --> 01:01:50.062
-[Jin-hyung] Wow. -[Jae-hee] Wow, look at that, son!

1211
01:01:50.145 --> 01:01:51.939
-Wow! -[dreamy, ethereal music playing]

1212
01:01:54.608 --> 01:01:57.402
[Jin-hyung] My balloon. Oh, no!

1213
01:01:57.486 --> 01:01:59.029
Whoa, honey!

1214
01:02:01.823 --> 01:02:02.824
[groans in pain]

1215
01:02:03.283 --> 01:02:04.243
[Jae-hee] Jin-hyung!

1216
01:02:05.244 --> 01:02:07.037
-[Jin-hyung] Thank you, sir. -[Jae-hee] Honey!

1217
01:02:08.497 --> 01:02:11.083
Papa. Papa, I'm over here.

1218
01:02:11.166 --> 01:02:14.253
[sighs] I told you not to run around in big crowds, honey.

1219
01:02:14.336 --> 01:02:15.462
Papa.

1220
01:02:15.546 --> 01:02:18.632
[dreamy, ethereal music continues]

1221
01:02:20.842 --> 01:02:21.760
Huh?

1222
01:02:22.886 --> 01:02:23.804
Son?

1223
01:02:24.388 --> 01:02:26.598
[fireworks exploding]

1224
01:02:26.682 --> 01:02:27.933
"Papa"?

1225
01:02:28.642 --> 01:02:32.145
[ethereal, soaring music playing]

1226
01:02:32.229 --> 01:02:33.772
[upbeat music playing]

1227
01:02:33.855 --> 01:02:35.148
[gasps]

1228
01:02:43.407 --> 01:02:47.327
LOVE IN DISGUISE

1229
01:02:47.411 --> 01:02:50.330
[closing theme music playing]

1230
01:03:09.391 --> 01:03:10.350
SPECIAL THANKS TO CHOI HEE-JIN, KIM DO-YOON, JUNG YOO-MIN,

1231
01:03:10.434 --> 01:03:11.351
PARK JUN-MUYN, YU SU-BIN FOR THEIR SPECIAL APPEARANCE

1232
01:03:11.935 --> 01:03:13.812
[Yi-jun] Kang Jae-hee, you were married?

1233
01:03:13.895 --> 01:03:15.981
[Jae-hee] My boss is acting really strange.

1234
01:03:16.064 --> 01:03:17.566
Stop making me worry.

1235
01:03:17.649 --> 01:03:18.817
Take it. You're cute.

1236
01:03:18.900 --> 01:03:20.110
I could buy the whole thing for you.

1237
01:03:20.193 --> 01:03:22.696
-That's how nice I am. -Do you like me?

1238
01:03:23.238 --> 01:03:25.449
-[Yi-jun] I'll meet up with him. -[Hye-jung] It has a built-in recorder.

1239
01:03:25.532 --> 01:03:27.159
[Si-hyun] I'll play whatever role you want,

1240
01:03:27.242 --> 01:03:29.202
your lawyer, your ex, so don't get cold feet.

1241
01:03:29.286 --> 01:03:31.747
Maybe I can afford to have Jae-hee by my side.

1242
01:03:31.830 --> 01:03:34.291
[Si-a] Sorry, but I have to reveal it. Mr. Kang is a woman.

1243
01:03:34.374 --> 01:03:35.542
[Yi-jun] What's the problem?

1244
01:03:35.626 --> 01:03:36.668
[Jae-hee] You should prioritize it over me.

1245
01:03:36.752 --> 01:03:38.629
That way I wouldn't get the wrong idea.

1246
01:03:38.712 --> 01:03:39.963
What?
